IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART III, "Standards", reg 63: the requirements that a Weekly
-- Indemnity Plan must meet. Layer 1 (the law, objectively), piece er4. Unofficial plain-text rendering; nothing here
-- is "verified against the official text". No section GIVEN: every rule has its own GIVEN.
--
-- THE SHAPE. One rule per paragraph (a) to (g), each reading the facts of one plan in one record, and one rule that
-- joins the seven. Regs 64, 65 and 66 (module er4-part3-regs64-66-other-plans) "satisfy all the requirements of
-- section 63, except 63(e) and (f)" and so CALL these paragraph rules; nothing is copied.
-- WHAT THE TEXT LEAVES TO JUDGMENT. Whether a plan's condition is "no wider than" one the paragraph lists (63(g)) is a
-- classification of the plan's own terms made by the person or the Commission; the constructors below carry the
-- limits the paragraph states (earnings under s 35, reinstatement on return, continuing treatment, six months).
-- "After three months" and the like are read as the longest wait the plan may impose (fork F5); on an hour-bank plan
-- the hour limb replaces the month limb (fork F6).

§ `Regulation 63 -- Weekly Indemnity Plan`

§§ `Regulation 63(f) and (g) -- the events and the conditions the paragraphs name (declared first: the record reads them)`

-- src:1051 | (f) in any case not referred to in paragraph (e) and subject to the elimination period referred to in paragraph (b), benefits are payable under the plan in respect of an illness or injury until the earliest of
-- src:1052 | (i) the end of a period of at least 15 weeks during which the benefits are paid,
-- src:1053 | (ii) the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury,
-- src:1054 | (iii) the date the insured person retires, and
-- src:1055 | (iv) the date of the insured person's separation from employment for any reason other than illness or injury, where notice of the separation was given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(f) (src:1051-1055)
DECLARE `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan` IS ONE OF
    `er4 the end of a period during which the benefits are paid`                    -- 63(f)(i), 64(d)(i), 65(f)(i), 66(e)(i)
    `er4 the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury`          -- (ii)
    `er4 the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave`                         -- 65(f)(iii), 66(e)(iii)
    `er4 the date the insured person retires`                                       -- 63(f)(iii)
    `er4 the date of the insured person's separation from employment for a reason other than illness or injury, notice having been given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury`   -- 63(f)(iv)
    `er4 any other event`                                                           -- not named by any paragraph

-- src:1056 | (g) the only conditions precluding the payment of benefits under the plan to an insured person to whom they would be otherwise payable are conditions that preclude payment to an insured person
-- src:1057 | (i) who is not under the care of a licensed physician,
-- src:1058 | (ii) whose illness or injury is covered by federal or provincial laws respecting workers' compensation, the Canada Pension Plan or An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan, where amounts paid under those laws or Acts constitute earnings under section 35,
-- src:1059 | (iii) whose illness or injury is intentionally self-inflicted,
-- src:1060 | (iv) whose illness or injury results from service in the armed forces,
-- src:1061 | (v) whose illness or injury results from war or participation in a riot or in a disturbance of the public order,
-- src:1062 | (vi) who becomes ill or is injured during a leave of absence or a period of paid vacation,
-- src:1063 | (vii) who is in receipt of benefits under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act,
-- src:1064 | (viii) whose illness or injury is sustained while committing a criminal offence,
-- src:1065 | (ix) who is engaged in employment for a wage or profit during any period for which the person claims benefits under the plan,
-- src:1066 | (x) who becomes ill or is injured after having lost employment by reason of a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the place where the person was employed, if the person's right to benefits under the plan is reinstated on their return to active employment,
-- src:1067 | (xi) who is an inmate of a prison or similar institution,
-- src:1068 | (xii) who is not entitled to benefits payable under the Act because the person is not in Canada,
-- src:1069 | (xiii) whose illness results from the use of drugs or alcohol and who is not receiving continuing treatment for the use of drugs or alcohol,
-- src:1070 | (xiv) whose illness or injury, resulting from a motor vehicle accident, is covered by a provincial plan described in paragraph 35(2)(d),
-- src:1071 | (xv) who is receiving a retirement pension from the employer,
-- src:1072 | (xvi) who is absent from work because of plastic surgery performed solely for cosmetic purposes, except where the need for surgery is attributable to an illness or injury, or
-- src:1073 | (xvii) who, in the case of a recurring disability, is receiving benefits under a group long-term disability plan that contains a reinstatement provision, where the reinstatement period under that plan does not exceed six months.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(g) (src:1056-1073)
DECLARE `er4 Condition that precludes payment of benefits under a plan` IS ONE OF
    `er4 the person is not under the care of a licensed physician`                                                  -- (i)
    `er4 the illness or injury is covered by workers' compensation law, the Canada Pension Plan or the Quebec Pension Plan`   -- (ii)
        HAS `er4 the plan applies the condition only where the amounts paid under those laws constitute earnings under section 35` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er4 the illness or injury is intentionally self-inflicted`                                                     -- (iii)
    `er4 the illness or injury results from service in the armed forces`                                            -- (iv)
    `er4 the illness or injury results from war or participation in a riot or in a disturbance of the public order` -- (v)
    `er4 the person becomes ill or is injured during a leave of absence or a period of paid vacation`              -- (vi)
    `er4 the person is in receipt of benefits under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act`                  -- (vii)
    `er4 the illness or injury is sustained while committing a criminal offence`                                    -- (viii)
    `er4 the person is engaged in employment for a wage or profit during a period for which the person claims benefits under the plan`   -- (ix)
    `er4 the person becomes ill or is injured after having lost employment by reason of a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the place where the person was employed`   -- (x)
        HAS `er4 the plan applies the condition only if the person's right to benefits under the plan is reinstated on their return to active employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er4 the person is an inmate of a prison or similar institution`                                                -- (xi)
    `er4 the person is not entitled to benefits payable under the Act because the person is not in Canada`          -- (xii)
    `er4 the illness results from the use of drugs or alcohol`                                                      -- (xiii)
        HAS `er4 the plan applies the condition only to a person not receiving continuing treatment for the use of drugs or alcohol` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er4 the illness or injury, resulting from a motor vehicle accident, is covered by a provincial plan described in paragraph 35(2)(d)`   -- (xiv)
    `er4 the person is receiving a retirement pension from the employer`                                            -- (xv)
    `er4 the person is absent from work because of plastic surgery performed solely for cosmetic purposes`          -- (xvi)
        HAS `er4 the plan excepts surgery needed because of an illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `er4 the person with a recurring disability is receiving benefits under a group long-term disability plan that contains a reinstatement provision`   -- (xvii)
        HAS `er4 the reinstatement period under that plan, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `er4 a condition not listed in paragraph 63(g)`                                                                 -- none of (i) to (xvii)

§§ `Regulation 63 -- the facts of one plan`

-- Everything regs 63(a) to (g) read. Months and hours, where a paragraph gives both, share one NUMBER whose unit is
-- months unless the plan is based on an hour-bank principle, when it is hours (fork F6).
-- src:1039 | 63 A Weekly Indemnity Plan shall meet the following requirements:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63 (src:1039)
DECLARE `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` HAS
    `er4 plan based on an hour-bank principle`                                            IS A BOOLEAN         -- 63(a)(ii), (e)
    `er4 day the employment commenced`                                                    IS A DATE            -- 63(a)(i)
    `er4 day the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan`                IS A DATE            -- 63(a)
    `er4 day the person has an accumulation of 400 hours of active employment`            IS A DATE            -- 63(a)(ii)
    `er4 plan requires an elimination period`                                             IS A BOOLEAN         -- 63(b)
    `er4 days in the elimination period`                                                  IS A NUMBER          -- 63(b)
    `er4 elimination period begins with the first day of the period of incapacity`        IS A BOOLEAN         -- 63(b)
    `er4 plan pays in full whatever benefits are payable under the Act`                   IS A BOOLEAN         -- 63(c)(i)
    `er4 plan pays in full whatever benefits are payable from another source that are not earnings under section 35`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- 63(c)(ii)
    `er4 weekly benefit payable under the plan`                                           IS A NUMBER          -- 63(d)
    `er4 normal weekly insurable earnings`                                                IS A NUMBER          -- 63(d)
    `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated on a recurrence`      IS A NUMBER          -- 63(e)(i)
    `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated for a new illness or injury`   IS A NUMBER   -- 63(e)(ii)
    `er4 longest period for which benefits are paid for one illness or injury, in weeks`  IS A NUMBER          -- 63(f)(i)
    `er4 events that end payment of benefits`                                             IS A LIST OF `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`   -- 63(f)
    `er4 conditions that preclude payment of benefits`                                    IS A LIST OF `er4 Condition that precludes payment of benefits under a plan`   -- 63(g)

§§ `Regulation 63(a) -- when the person becomes eligible`

-- src:1040 | (a) an insured person who is employed by an employer and covered by the plan becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in respect of an illness or injury on or before the first day of the month following
-- src:1041 | (i) the last day of a period of not more than three months of continuous employment beginning on the day of commencement of the employment, or
-- src:1042 | (ii) if the plan is based on an hour-bank principle, the day on which the person has an accumulation of not more than 400 hours of active employment;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(a)(i) (src:1040-1041)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 63(a)(i) the last day of a period of three months of continuous employment beginning on` d MEANS
    Date ((Day (`add months` d 3)) MINUS 1)

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(a) (src:1040-1042)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 63(a) the first day of the month following` d MEANS
    `add months` (YMD (DATE_YEAR d) (DATE_MONTH d) 1) 1

-- Limb (i) governs a plan not based on an hour-bank principle; limb (ii), "if the plan is based on an hour-bank
-- principle", governs one that is (fork F6). The person must be eligible on or before the first day of the month
-- following the day the limb names.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(a) (src:1040-1042)
GIVEN c IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(a) the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in time` c IF
    BRANCH IF c's `er4 plan based on an hour-bank principle`
           THEN c's `er4 day the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan`
                    AT MOST `reg 63(a) the first day of the month following` (c's `er4 day the person has an accumulation of 400 hours of active employment`)
           OTHERWISE c's `er4 day the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan`
                    AT MOST `reg 63(a) the first day of the month following` (`reg 63(a)(i) the last day of a period of three months of continuous employment beginning on` (c's `er4 day the employment commenced`))

§§ `Regulation 63(b) -- the elimination period`

-- src:1043 | (b) if an insured person is required to serve an elimination period during which no benefit is payable under the plan, that period does not exceed seven consecutive days beginning with the first day of the period of incapacity due to illness or injury;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(b) (src:1043)
GIVEN c IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(b) any elimination period does not exceed seven consecutive days beginning with the first day of the period of incapacity` c IF
        (NOT c's `er4 plan requires an elimination period`)
    OR  (    c's `er4 days in the elimination period` AT MOST 7
         AND c's `er4 elimination period begins with the first day of the period of incapacity`)

§§ `Regulation 63(c) -- benefits paid in full`

-- src:1044 | (c) benefits are paid in full under the plan regardless of
-- src:1045 | (i) the amount of the benefits that are payable to an insured person under the Act, and
-- src:1046 | (ii) the amount of the benefits, payable from any other source, that do not constitute earnings under section 35;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(c) (src:1044-1046)
GIVEN c IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(c) benefits are paid in full regardless of the benefits payable under the Act and from other sources` c IF
        c's `er4 plan pays in full whatever benefits are payable under the Act`
    AND c's `er4 plan pays in full whatever benefits are payable from another source that are not earnings under section 35`

§§ `Regulation 63(d) -- at least 55% of normal weekly insurable earnings`

-- src:1047 | (d) the benefits payable to an insured person under the plan are equivalent to an amount that is equal to or greater than 55% of the insured person's normal weekly insurable earnings;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(d) (src:1047)
GIVEN c IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(d) the benefits payable under the plan are at least 55% of the normal weekly insurable earnings` c IF
    c's `er4 weekly benefit payable under the plan` AT LEAST (c's `er4 normal weekly insurable earnings` TIMES 55%)

§§ `Regulation 63(e) -- reinstatement of full benefits`

-- src:1048 | (e) subject to the elimination period referred to in paragraph (b), full benefits payable to an insured person under the plan are reinstated
-- src:1049 | (i) in the case of the recurrence of an illness or injury, after three months of active employment following their most recent absence due to that illness or injury or, where the plan is based on an hour-bank principle, after the accumulation of the first 400 hours of active employment by that person following their most recent absence due to that illness or injury, and
-- src:1050 | (ii) in the case of a new illness or injury, after one month of active employment following their most recent absence due to another illness or injury or, where the plan is based on an hour-bank principle, after the accumulation of the first 150 hours of active employment by that person following their most recent absence due to another illness or injury;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(e)(i) (src:1048-1049)
GIVEN c IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(e)(i) full benefits are reinstated in time on the recurrence of an illness or injury` c IF
    BRANCH IF c's `er4 plan based on an hour-bank principle`
           THEN c's `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated on a recurrence` AT MOST 400
           OTHERWISE c's `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated on a recurrence` AT MOST 3

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(e)(ii) (src:1050)
GIVEN c IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(e)(ii) full benefits are reinstated in time for a new illness or injury` c IF
    BRANCH IF c's `er4 plan based on an hour-bank principle`
           THEN c's `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated for a new illness or injury` AT MOST 150
           OTHERWISE c's `er4 active employment after which full benefits are reinstated for a new illness or injury` AT MOST 1

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(e) (src:1048-1050)
GIVEN c IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(e) full benefits are reinstated as the paragraph requires` c IF
        `reg 63(e)(i) full benefits are reinstated in time on the recurrence of an illness or injury` c
    AND `reg 63(e)(ii) full benefits are reinstated in time for a new illness or injury` c

§§ `Regulation 63(f) -- benefits payable until the earliest of four events`

-- (i) "the end of a period of at least 15 weeks during which the benefits are paid" is read as: the plan pays for at
-- least 15 weeks; (ii) to (iv) are the other events at which a plan may stop. Any other event ending payment is a
-- stop the paragraph does not allow (fork F7).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(f) (src:1051-1055)
GIVEN event IS A `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(f) an event at which payment under the plan may end` event IF
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `er4 the end of a period during which the benefits are paid` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the date the insured person retires` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er4 the date of the insured person's separation from employment for a reason other than illness or injury, notice having been given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(f) (src:1051-1055)
GIVEN c IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` c IF
        c's `er4 longest period for which benefits are paid for one illness or injury, in weeks` AT LEAST 15
    AND all `reg 63(f) an event at which payment under the plan may end` (c's `er4 events that end payment of benefits`)

§§ `Regulation 63(g) -- the only conditions that may preclude payment`

-- src:1056 | (g) the only conditions precluding the payment of benefits under the plan to an insured person to whom they would be otherwise payable are conditions that preclude payment to an insured person
-- A plan's own condition counts as one of the seventeen only if it is no wider than the paragraph's, limits included;
-- a condition that fits none of them is `er4 a condition not listed in paragraph 63(g)`.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(g) (src:1056-1073)
GIVEN condition IS A `er4 Condition that precludes payment of benefits under a plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` condition IF
    CONSIDER condition
    WHEN `er4 the illness or injury is covered by workers' compensation law, the Canada Pension Plan or the Quebec Pension Plan` limited THEN limited
    WHEN `er4 the person becomes ill or is injured after having lost employment by reason of a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the place where the person was employed` limited THEN limited
    WHEN `er4 the illness results from the use of drugs or alcohol` limited THEN limited
    WHEN `er4 the person is absent from work because of plastic surgery performed solely for cosmetic purposes` limited THEN limited
    WHEN `er4 the person with a recurring disability is receiving benefits under a group long-term disability plan that contains a reinstatement provision` months THEN months AT MOST 6
    WHEN `er4 a condition not listed in paragraph 63(g)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63(g) (src:1056-1073)
GIVEN c IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63(g) the only conditions precluding payment are conditions the paragraph lists` c IF
    all `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (c's `er4 conditions that preclude payment of benefits`)

§§ `Regulation 63 -- all seven requirements`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 63 (src:1039-1073)
GIVEN c IS A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` c IF
        `reg 63(a) the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in time` c
    AND `reg 63(b) any elimination period does not exceed seven consecutive days beginning with the first day of the period of incapacity` c
    AND `reg 63(c) benefits are paid in full regardless of the benefits payable under the Act and from other sources` c
    AND `reg 63(d) the benefits payable under the plan are at least 55% of the normal weekly insurable earnings` c
    AND `reg 63(e) full benefits are reinstated as the paragraph requires` c
    AND `reg 63(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` c
    AND `reg 63(g) the only conditions precluding payment are conditions the paragraph lists` c
